## Required tests and delivery evidence

- Real bare remote already at v2: two distinct successful native publications;
  remote records/map/checkpoint/history and private commit/tree receipts match.
  Completed retry is NOOP; mathematical stages and foreign files/index unchanged.
- Required complete-path regression: construct the map from actual pinned Git
  BASE blobs, run the EXISTING evidence intake(map) through its real INTENT and
  CONFIRMED checkpoints, then save publication INTENT, reserve, perform guarded
  ordinary merge/commit/push and confirm. No magically preexisting map or mocked
  intake/checkpoint transition. Assert BASE metadata hashes stay immutable while
  each live revision changes, all intermediate history survives, and the private
  snapshot binds the final publication-INTENT bytes. A stale pins.head or a HEAD
  change between map construction/intake and publication admission fails closed.
- 45 records, 127 incoming files, and their combined case: external maps,
  RESUME <=8192, full hashes covered. Use a REAL incoming branch and merge;
  incoming tip/all ancestry remain ancestors of published commit, no copied tree.
- Mismatch matrix: owner/epoch/base/endpoint, map/predecessor/history drift,
  final bytes/Git blobs/modes, undeclared paths, dirty/staged overlap, lost private
  state. Admission rejection changes no worktree/index/branch/remote; permitted
  observation may fetch objects only, not refs/FETCH_HEAD.
- Crash before reservation permits fresh retry. Crash after reservation, during
  local merge/commit, after commit, after consumed push intent, or after server
  acceptance yields original-operation inspection, not replay. Preserve partial
  state when UNKNOWN. Two competing callers cannot consume the same push twice.
- Real subprocess kill after a bare remote accepted the push; fresh-process
  reconciliation confirms original pinned commit/tree with no additional push.
  Pending marker fences unrelated writers even with changed mutable control.
- Remote advancement/non-fast-forward, lost client output and endpoint drift
  never force, renew, broaden scope or falsely confirm.
- Regression: initial bootstrap v1-only behavior, generic source-only publication,
  other native effects, launch/intake and checkpoint tests unchanged. Targeted
  tests first; then affected workflow suite and tool-manifest wiring. No unrelated
  Lean run or repetition of prior no-change acceptance work.
- Actual issue lifecycle in the bare-remote fixture: confirmed HIGH publication
  bug -> independently verified exact repair -> real named local commit -> real
  ordinary remote publication/readback -> FIX_COMMITTED/FIX_PUSH_VERIFIED as
  supported by existing event ordering. Publication cannot require falsely closing
  this issue first. Wrong repair subject, candidate hash, review identity or extra
  payload paths stay held; unrelated affected effects stay held throughout.
- Parent's independent checker reviews this exact plan before implementation.
  Mode A: no unresolved substantive findings and two on-target WORDING-only/empty
  passes; immutable CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW/WORDING/OFF-TARGET/TOOL-FAILURE labels.
  Then exact final artifact review, actual owner integration/readback, only needed
  derived refresh and named ordinary publication. Isolated tests alone never
  claim canonical deployment or mathematical acceptance.
